 [:db/cas 17592186364171 :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=4,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} &={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2} &={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3} &={a}_{3}-5{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$" "$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=4,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} &={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2} &={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3} &={a}_{3}-5{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$"]
 [:db/cas 17592186364171 :question/worked-solution "First, we normalize the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{3}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{4}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{2}=4{q}_{2} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{3}}{2}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{3}=2{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the set ${{q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}}$ will be both orthogonal and normalized.\n\nNext, let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} &={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2} &={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3} &={a}_{3}-5{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} &={v}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} &=3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=9{q}_{1}+4{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} &=5{v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}+{v}_{3}=15{q}_{1}+8{q}_{2}+2{q}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe final system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}=15+4+2=21.\n$$" "First, we normalize the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{3}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{4}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{2}=4{q}_{2} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{{v}_{3}}{2}\\,⟹\\,{v}_{3}=2{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the set ${{q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}}$ will be both orthogonal and normalized.\n\nNext, let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\