 [:db/cas 17592186379070 :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is irrational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $4$ divide to $10$ or $16.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ divides }10}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{4\\text{ divides }16}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\pi \\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{4\\text{ divides }10\\text{ or }16}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧(Q∨R).$" "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is irrational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $4$ divide to $10$ or $16.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }10}_{Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }16}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\pi \\text{ is irrational}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }10\\text{ or }16}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧(Q∨R).$"]
 [:db/cas 17592186379077 :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $10$ is composite or even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{10\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{10\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $8$ is divisible by $2$ or $6.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{8\\text{ is divisible by 2}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{8\\text{ is divisible by }6}_{⏟}}_{D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $C∨D.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{10\\text{ is composite }\\text{or}\\text{ even}}_{⏟}}_{A\\,∨\\,B}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{8\\text{ is divisible by }2\\text{ or }6}_{⏟}}_{C\\,∨\\,D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∨B)∧(C∨D).$" "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $10$ is composite or even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{10\\text{ is composite}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{10\\text{ is even }}_{B}\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $8$ is divisible by $2$ or $6.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by 2}}_{C}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by }6}_{D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $C∨D.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{10\\text{ is composite }\\text{or}\\text{ even}}_{A\\,∨\\,B}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by }2\\text{ or }6}_{C\\,∨\\,D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∨B)∧(C∨D).$"]
