 [:db/cas 17592186389670 :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $n$  is negative or greater than $10.$  This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is negative }}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{n\\text{ is greater than }10}_{⏟}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨G.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $n$ is odd. This corresponds to $O.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is negative }\\text{ or }\\text{ greater than }10}_{⏟}}_{N∨G}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{n\\text{ is odd }}_{⏟}}_{O},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∨G)∧O.$" "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $n$  is negative or greater than $10.$  This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{n\\text{ is negative }}_{N}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{n\\text{ is greater than }10}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨G.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $n$ is odd. This corresponds to $O.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{n\\text{ is negative }\\text{ or }\\text{ greater than }10}_{N∨G}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{n\\text{ is odd }}_{O},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∨G)∧O.$"]
