 [:db/cas 17592186389724 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{10\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{10\\text{ is even}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"]
