 [:db/cas 17592186429896 :question/worked-solution "The square of $3$ is the same as ${3}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${3}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}={{3\\times 3}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The square of $3$ is the same as ${3}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${3}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}=\\underbrace{3\\times 3}_{2\\text{ times}}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$"]
 [:db/cas 17592186429897 :question/worked-solution "Here, $9$ raised to the power of $3$ means ${9}^{3}.$\n\nTo compute this power, we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{9}^{3}={{9\\times 9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $9\\times 9=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{81}\\times 9 & =81\\times 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $81\\times 9.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $81\\times 9=729,$ then ${9}^{3}=729.$" "Here, $9$ raised to the power of $3$ means ${9}^{3}.$\n\nTo compute this power, we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{9}^{3}=\\underbrace{9\\times 9\\times 9}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $9\\times 9=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{9\\times 9}_{81}\\times 9 & =81\\times 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $81\\times 9.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $81\\times 9=729,$ then ${9}^{3}=729.$"]
