 [:db/cas 17592186429904 :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate ${10}^{3}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${10}^{3},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{10}^{3}={{10\\times 10\\times 10}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $10\\times 10=100,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{10\\times 10}_{⏟}}_{100}\\times 10 & =100\\times 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $100\\times 10=1,000,$ we have ${10}^{3}=1,000.$" "We need to evaluate ${10}^{3}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${10}^{3},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{10}^{3}=\\underbrace{10\\times 10\\times 10}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $10\\times 10=100,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{10\\times 10}_{100}\\times 10 & =100\\times 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $100\\times 10=1,000,$ we have ${10}^{3}=1,000.$"]
