e matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=-3-6x.$"]
